# Model config: Qwen3.8-27B (BF16, sharded GGUF) -- model-intrinsic only.
#
# 27B hybrid-attention VL model (Apache 2.0). Arch string in the GGUF is
# `qwen35`. Standard ggml-org/llama.cpp master is sufficient -- the
# unslothai `iq1-narrow` branch is only needed for the sub-IQ1_S dtypes used
# by the 2.4T model, not for this one.
#
# Verified from the GGUF metadata (2026-08-14), which corrects a couple of
# numbers in the upstream write-up:
#   block_count            65      (64 transformer layers + 1 MTP/nextn head)
#   full_attention_interval 4      -> 16 of 65 blocks are full attention;
#                                     the rest are Gated DeltaNet (SSM state,
#                                     constant size, NOT part of the KV cache)
#   head_count 24 / head_count_kv 4 (GQA 6:1), key_length = value_length = 256
#   embedding_length 5120, feed_forward_length 17408
#   context_length 262144, rope.freq_base 1e7, rope.dimension_count 64
# KV cost therefore is 16 x 4 x 256 x 2 = 32,768 elements/token
#   -> ~34 KiB/token at q8_0 (~64 KiB/token at f16).
# That is ~2.7x Qwen3-Coder-Next's per-token KV, so budget context carefully;
# the per-machine profiles under profiles/<machine>/qwen3.8-27b*.env do that.
#
# WEIGHTS: BF16 is sharded; point -m at the FIRST shard, llama.cpp loads the
# rest. 46.55 + 4.35 = ~50.9 GiB of weights.
#
# NOTE ON LAYOUT: unlike the other models in this repo, these quants sit at the
# model directory root rather than in per-quant subfolders (that is how they
# were downloaded). The BF16 shards do live in a BF16/ subfolder.
#
# VISION: native image+video VL. The multimodal projector is a separate file
# and must be passed with --mmproj or the server is text-only. Paired here with
# the BF16 projector to match BF16 weights; the quantized configs use F16.
#
# Sampling -- THINKING mode, which is the default for this model (it emits
# <think>...</think> before the answer). Values from the Qwen model card, and
# the temp/top-p/top-k trio is corroborated by the GGUF's own
# general.sampling.* keys (temp 1.0, top_p 0.95, top_k 20):
#   temp 1.0, top-p 0.95, top-k 20, min-p 0.0, presence-penalty 0.0,
#   repeat-penalty 1.0
# llama.cpp defaults min-p to 0.05, so 0.0 must be set explicitly.
# For INSTRUCT / non-thinking use qwen3.8-27b-instruct.env instead.
#
# Thinking control (pass through the API, not the CLI) via chat_template_kwargs:
#   {"enable_thinking": false}      -> disable thinking
#   {"preserve_thinking": false}    -> drop prior-turn reasoning (cheaper, but
#                                      worse KV reuse / agentic consistency)
#   "reasoning_effort": xhigh (default) | medium | low
# Lowering reasoning_effort does NOT reliably cut end-to-end agentic latency --
# shallower analysis just causes retries.
#
# Output budgeting (agentic): reasoning up to 262,144 tokens, final response up
# to 131,072. A context smaller than that will truncate long reasoning chains.

: "${MODEL:=Qwen3.8-27B/BF16/Qwen3.8-27B-BF16-00001-of-00002.gguf}"

LLAMA_ARGS+=(--temp 1.0 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --min-p 0.0 --presence-penalty 0.0 --repeat-penalty 1.0)
LLAMA_ARGS+=(--mmproj "/models/Qwen3.8-27B/mmproj-BF16.gguf")
LLAMA_ARGS+=(--alias qwen3.8-27b)
